  "request": {
    "spec": "A person can have plans: an amount, a start date, every N days (a whole number, at least 1) and an\nend date, from a form on the row (PLAN_ADDED name=<name> amount=<amount> start=<date>\nevery=<n> end=<date>; an end before the start or a bad amount or interval is refused with an error\non the row). A generate button on the screen makes, for every plan on the sheet in the order they\nwere added, a DRAFT claim with the plan's amount for every plan date (the start, then every N days)\nup to the end and the sheet's today that has none yet, dated that day with an empty note, by the\nclaim form's rules (a date the form refuses is skipped and tried again next time). Show how many\nwere made, and on each plan how many claims it has made so far.\n",
    "prompt": "You are implementing ONE change to this application.\n\nFIRST read AGENTS.md \u2014 it states the working rules and how the app is tested, and sends you to\nDESIGN.md for the app's stack and conventions. Follow both.\n\nTHE CHANGE REQUEST:\nA person can have plans: an amount, a start date, every N days (a whole number, at least 1) and an\nend date, from a form on the row (PLAN_ADDED name=<name> amount=<amount> start=<date>\nevery=<n> end=<date>; an end before the start or a bad amount or interval is refused with an error\non the row). A generate button on the screen makes, for every plan on the sheet in the order they\nwere added, a DRAFT claim with the plan's amount for every plan date (the start, then every N days)\nup to the end and the sheet's today that has none yet, dated that day with an empty note, by the\nclaim form's rules (a date the form refuses is skipped and tried again next time). Show how many\nwere made, and on each plan how many claims it has made so far.\n\nYour work is verified by an automated Playwright UI test already installed under e2e/specs/.\nRead that spec: it declares the exact data-testid anchors, values, test data and any audit\nrecords it expects \u2014 match them. Run `bin/e2e` to build the app, start it, and run the test as\nyou work; iterate until it passes. Change whatever the request needs across the app \u2014 its stored\ndata, its server and its front end. Do NOT edit bin/build, bin/start, bin/stop, bin/e2e,\nAGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, DESIGN.md, e2e/support/ or the test spec.\n"
  },
