    "result_text": "I added plans and plan-claim generation, and all 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass: the main plans test and the three scenario tests.\n\n**What it does**\n- **Adding a plan:** each person row has a plan form for amount, start, every N days and end. It refuses an amount that is negative or has more than two decimals, an interval below 1, and an end before the start. A refusal shows the error on the row and writes nothing. A plan that goes through writes `PLAN_ADDED \u2026 name= amount= start= every= end=` to the audit file. The row lists each plan with a count of the claims it has made so far.\n- **Generating:** a \"Generate plan claims\" button goes through the sheet's plans in the order they were added. For each plan date (the start, then every N days) up to the earlier of the plan's end and the sheet's today, it makes a DRAFT claim with the plan's amount and an empty note, if that date has none yet. It shows how many claims it made.\n- **Refused dates:** each claim goes through the normal claim-add rules (closed periods, retirement and so on). Each claim is saved on its own, so a refused date changes nothing, the other dates still go through, and the refused date is tried again on the next generate.\n- **Avoiding duplicates:** each plan keeps the dates it has already made a claim for, and that list is also where the \"made so far\" count comes from.\n\n**Where it is**\n- The database change is `V73__plan.sql`, which adds the `plan` and `plan_claim` tables.\n- The server code is in the new `plan/` package.\n- The screen code is the new `features/plans/plans.ts`, plus the generate button and wiring in `people.ts`.\n\n**Changes to existing features you might not expect**\n- **Merging people:** when a person is merged into another, their plans now move to the person they were merged into.\n- **Transferring a person:** when a person is transferred to another sheet, their plans are deleted, because plans belong to one sheet.\n- **Cloning a sheet:** a clone does not copy plans. The request didn't say what should happen, so I left cloning unchanged.",
